WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.421
- We have an audience question
for the cast. Where is Cruz?

00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:04.254
- [Cruz] Right here, right here.

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.087
- [Clarkson] What's up Cruz?

00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:05.920
- Hi, how's it going?

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.410
- [Clarkson] You can stand
up, what's your question?

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.550
- Okay, so I have a question for you guys.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.710
So, I'm obviously a big Marvel fan,

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.280
and it has taught me a lot of
really valuable life lessons.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.320
But, I want to know
what has it taught you?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.510
Like being part of the Marvel Universe.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.730
- Oh, Elizabeth would
you like to go first?

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:25.620
- Sure, well, I think the
character I play, Wanda.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.560
She's made lots of,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.093
she's very opinionated and through that,

00:00:31.093 --> 00:00:34.350
has also found herself making mistakes.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.640
And I think it's important for us

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.400
to watch people make mistakes.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.780
I mean I think do that pretty well

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.130
with a lot of our characters.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:45.713
And I think it's important
to show that kind of process,

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:49.950
working through suffering of
different kinds, from that.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.660
And, so I guess it's-
- [Kelly] It's real.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.920
- Yeah, so it's been,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.561
I think I have appreciated
getting to explore that

00:00:55.561 --> 00:00:57.150
through this.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:57.983
- [Clarkson] Yeah.

00:00:57.983 --> 00:01:00.071
- What about you, Benedict C?
(Gomez chuckling)

00:01:00.071 --> 00:01:01.170
- Benedict C, yeah, it's again

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.310
through the character, I guess.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.900
I mean, through making a Marvel film,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.910
you learn, a lot.
(laughing)

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.490
A lot to do with patience
and pacing yourself.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.440
- Lots of patience.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.350
- But also, I think the
characters do always,

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.880
that's what's great about
them. There's great laughs,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.770
there's great action,
there's sort of enticement

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.450
for a spectacle, as you know.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.760
But, there's also
something of the Zeitgeist

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.900
or something profound to takeaway.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.970
For me, for him, especially in this one,

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.730
it's learning that you
are stronger together

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.410
than you are on your own.
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.610
- It's pretty much the lesson I carry away

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.643
from this one, without
giving away too much.

00:01:30.643 --> 00:01:32.319
- [Kelly] Boy, drive that
one home for the world.

00:01:32.319 --> 00:01:34.238
- [Olsen] Yeah.
- [Clarkson] Yeah. (laughing)

00:01:34.238 --> 00:01:35.880
Listen!
- Yes. Yes.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.790
- What about you, Benedict W? (chuckling)

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.370
- I've just enjoyed
overall, what Marvel do,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.650
with these incredible films, you know,

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.480
it's about inclusion and how we represent

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.980
many people, of color.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.040
And again, as I talked about the platform

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.899
and opportunities that
we have with 'Shang-Chi'

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:56.732
and now,
- Oh, I love.

00:01:56.732 --> 00:01:57.870
- we have 'Miss Marvel' coming up

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:01.320
and everybody gets to see
that they can have a hero

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.660
that they can follow, so.
- Absolutely.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.493
- I love, yeah.

00:02:04.493 --> 00:02:07.410
- So, it's so important
because I think a lot

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.361
of times people are like, you know,

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:11.010
they want to see themselves,
but also it's important

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.020
for other people to see
other people in these roles.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.070
- [Cruz] Yeah.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.720
- [Clarkson] That's
the bigger picture too,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.850
is like, to make sure
you're seeing everyone

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.590
for those kids, as well.
- Yeah.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.120
- [Clarkson] Marvel does
such a great job with that,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.313
I feel like.
- Yeah.

